# Portfolio site

- Interactive portfolio for Daniel A Rodrigues, presented as one system with two interfaces over a single shared content source: a scrollable web UI and a contextual AI assistant that lives in a centered terminal modal. The assistant is Daniel's assistant (it speaks about him, not as him) and can be opened generally or scoped to a specific project/role. Current features: streaming chat (OpenRouter via Route Handlers) with optional project/experience context, MongoDB-backed threaded messages with TTL, project detail routes for all projects, resume download, experience timeline, skills, and about.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind + shadcn/ui (`new-york`, themeable `surface-*` CSS variables, dark `color-scheme`, sage `glow` accent)
- Fonts: Geist (body) + Instrument Serif (`--font-display`, headings) + JetBrains Mono (`--font-mono`, tech labels/metadata/terminal)
- Backend: Route Handlers under `src/app/api/v1` + `src/server/` (MongoDB, OpenRouter)
- HTTP (client): native `fetch` + ReadableStream for chat SSE
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`
- Skill logos: path data in `@src/shared/skillIcons.ts` (do not import the `simple-icons` package barrel — it is a multi-MB module); skills currently render as grouped typography without icons

## Layout

- App shell: `@src/app/layout.tsx` renders `@src/app/components/app-shell.tsx`, which wraps every route (home + `/projects/[slug]`) in `ChatProvider`, plus `ThemeBackground`, `Navbar`, and `@src/app/components/ui/lazy-overlays.tsx` (loads the terminal overlay only after first open). `@src/app/page.tsx` renders only the homepage sections. Contact (email/GitHub/LinkedIn/resume) lives in `ContactSection` (`#contact`), not a global footer.
- Home page composition: `Hero` (status line + serif headline) → `ExperienceTimeline` (`#experience`; each role's Details expands to highlights plus compact work-project summaries that link to `/projects/<slug>`) → `ProjectsSection` (`#projects`, personal projects only — compact two-column grid of equal-height entries with a clamped description, capped tech list, and no inline metrics; metrics and the full case study live on `/projects/<slug>`) → `SkillsGrid` (`#skills`) → `AboutSection` (`#about`, bio plus quiet chat entry) → `OutsideWork` → `ContactSection` (`#contact`)
- UI: `@src/app/components/ui/` — shadcn primitives plus `navbar`, `hero`, `chat-provider`, `ask-daniel-button`, `theme-background`, `projects-section`, `experience-timeline`, `skills-grid`, `about-section`, `outside-work`, `contact-section`, `tracked-anchor`, `lazy-overlays`, `analytics-tracker`, `scroll`
- Terminal UI: `@src/app/components/terminal/fullscreen-terminal.tsx` (default export, lazy-loaded centered modal). Opened via `useChat().openChat()` from the navbar TerminalSquare control, Ask Daniel buttons, and the about-section CTA. The transcript is the chat thread (`Message[]`); there is no command registry. Do not re-add an inline hero terminal or a sidebar chat panel.
- Project routes: `@src/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx` — server-rendered, `generateStaticParams` + per-page metadata for every project in `PROJECTS`. Work projects still list under the owning role in `ExperienceTimeline` (`relatedExperienceId`); Details navigates to `/projects/<slug>`. Personal projects are listed in `ProjectsSection` and use the same detail route.
- Content (client-safe): `@src/shared/profile.ts` (profile, experience, skills, interests, education as `{ period, degree, institution, focus?, activities?, highlights? }[]`, nav links) and `@src/shared/projects.ts` (`PROJECTS` for all projects, `PERSONAL_PROJECTS`, `getProjectsByExperienceId`, `Project` type with `origin: "work" | "personal"` plus optional `metrics` and `visual` for editorial layouts)
- Project visuals: when a personal project gets a screenshot/diagram, save it as `public/images/projects/<slug>.png` (or `.webp`; 16:9, ~1600×900, optimized) and set `visual: { src: "/images/projects/<slug>.png", alt: "..." }` on that project in `projects.ts` — `ProjectsSection` renders it as a 16:9 thumbnail in the grid; `@src/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx` renders it large. No component changes needed.
- API routes: `@src/app/api/v1/`
- Server logic: `@src/server/` (`db/`, `chat/`, `ai/` including `systemPrompt.ts` and `context.ts`)
- Client API helpers: `@src/shared/` (`api.ts`, `endpoints.ts`, `config.ts`)
- Chat state: `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts` exposed through `ChatProvider` (context-aware: open/close, retry, contextType/contextId). Overlay open state lives here; there is no separate terminal provider.
- Utils: `@src/lib/utils.ts` (`cn`), `@src/lib/sourceLinks.ts` (AI navigation link markers), `@src/lib/contactCta.ts` (contact CTA marker)

## Theming

- Single dark look via `html.dark` and tokens in `@src/app/globals.css`
- Colors: use `surface-*` and `glow` (sage accent) / semantic tokens — never hardcode `zinc-*` or raw hex
- Editorial style: whitespace and hairline `border-surface-800/70` dividers instead of cards; headings use `font-display` (Instrument Serif); mono reserved for tech labels, metadata, terminal
- Mono text (terminal, tech lists, metadata) uses `font-mono` → `--font-mono` (JetBrains Mono)
- Ambient page background: `@src/app/components/ui/theme-background.tsx`
- Do not reintroduce album/music theme switching unless explicitly requested

## Guardrails

- Extend `@src/shared/` for browser→API calls; do not invent parallel fetch wrappers
- Put server-only backend logic under `@src/server/` and Route Handlers under `@src/app/api/`
- Keep portfolio content in `@src/shared/profile.ts` / `@src/shared/projects.ts` in sync with facts in `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` when bio/experience/project changes — `systemPrompt.ts` interpolates dates/roles/tech/impact from those shared modules rather than duplicating them
- Preserve the dark portfolio UX; style with `surface-*` / `glow` tokens rather than one-off color classes
- LLM calls go through OpenRouter (see `@v2-migration.mdc`); never put API keys in client code
- Do not reintroduce Telegram notify or title-generation endpoints unless explicitly requested
- New unit tests go under `tests/` (mirror `src/` paths; see `vitest-tests.mdc`); CI runs lint, typecheck, unit tests, and build on PRs and `main` (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`); keep PR descriptions short using `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`
- LLM answer quality evals live under `evals/` and run with `npm run eval` (manual, paid OpenRouter calls — never CI). See `vitest-tests.mdc`.
- After large features/redesigns, update `.cursor/rules/` in the same PR (`keep-rules-in-sync.mdc`; workflow skill `.cursor/skills/sync-cursor-rules/`)
